ut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John C. Hadjipateras | Chairman of the Board, President & CEO | Age 75 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 602 people. Revenue per employee of $800K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Dorian LPG Ltd. is a mid-cap energy business with a $2.1B market cap on $482M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 4.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $9.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 28% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 35% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Learn Why The Bull Case For Dorian LPG (LPG) Could Change Following Irregular Cash Dividend","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-lpg/doriang/news/learn-why-the-bull-case-for-dorian-lpg-lpg-could-change-foll","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575790.633,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (LPG) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_LPG_Edition_111226093002_1794493802.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794493802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Dorian LPG (NYSE:LPG) Cut to Buy at Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/dorian-lpg-nyselpg-cut-to-buy-at-wall-street-zen.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp