ear).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.05 across 203 companies in the universe; the top four hold 40% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 140% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 20% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 42% and a beta of 0.92, it moves roughly with the market.","About $28.8M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 60% in the 2020 crash and 24% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 23% below its blended-model fair value of $62.58, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 2%).","On multiples it looks cheap against Energy peers: P/E 4.3 vs 13.6 and EV/EBITDA 4.5 vs 7.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 40% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an EBIT/EV of 10.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 5 covering analysts target $57.20 on average, 19% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 11% earns above the cost of capital of 8.2%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.89).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.09x.","ROE of 17% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.6x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 13pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 2.3% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.8x net debt to EBITDA ($327.4M of cash against $560.4M of debt), with interest covered 7.2x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.67)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 7.3% over 3 years and 8.8% over 5 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 41%).","Free cash flow has compounded 22.2% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 74%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.1x, 17.6% of sales), a maintenance pace."],"own":["Insiders own 14.0%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 76%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (12 sales, net $9.5M sold).","It returns 5.4% a year to shareholders (0.3% in buybacks and 8.2% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.4% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 602 employees, each generates about $800K of revenue, 0.4x the Energy median, and revenue has grown 14.9% a year across its filed history.","CEO pay is $3.4M (4x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $18K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":89,"head":"Invest: trades 23% below fair value of $62.58; revenue grew 8.8%/yr over 5y.","pros":["Composite 42, above the 39 line (gates 12/26)","Trades 23% below fair value of $62.58","Revenue grew 8.8%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.8x","P/E 4.3x vs sector 13.6x"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":53.19,"vc":{"base":62.58,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":62.58,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.0174,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":13.5876,"ev_ebitda":7.146,"pfcf":14.6331,"pb":1.7432,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0762,"div_yield":0.0357}},"ticker":"LPG","date":"2026-11-13"}